RAWPANEL(1)

# NAME

rawpanel - persistent rawmkit desktop panel

# SYNOPSIS

*rawpanel* [*-c* _FILE_] [*-C*] [*--status-debug*] [*-v*]

# DESCRIPTION

*rawpanel* presents rawm's authoritative monitor, tag, layout, focused-title,
and admitted-stack state. It acquires machine status independently and owns the
XEmbed system-tray selection. Panel windows are EWMH docks and reserve work
area with standard struts.
The tray follows the XEmbed mapped flag; when no mapped tray icon is present it reserves no visible panel cell.

rawpanel is not a window manager and does not reconstruct rawm state from EWMH
client lists. Focused-title presentation comes from rawm's authoritative
*\_RAWM\_CLIENTS* inventory rather than direct client-property observation.
Refreshing that state may redraw or resize an already mapped dock, but does not
raise it; managed/fullscreen stacking remains rawm authority.

# OPTIONS

*-c* _FILE_
	Apply exactly _FILE_ to built-in defaults, bypassing the normal system and
	user configuration files.

*-C*
	Validate configuration and exit without opening X11.

*--status-debug*
	Run the configured native status sources in the foreground and print semantic snapshots without opening X11.

*-v*
	Print version and exit.

*-h*
	Print usage and exit.

# CONFIGURATION

Without *-c*, rawpanel layers built-in defaults, the system file
_${SYSCONFDIR}/rawpanel/rawpanel.conf_ (normally
_/etc/rawpanel/rawpanel.conf_), then the user file from
_$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/rawpanel/rawpanel.conf_ when *XDG_CONFIG_HOME* is absolute,
or _$HOME/.config/rawpanel/rawpanel.conf_ otherwise. Missing default files are
allowed.

Unknown settings and settings with the wrong type fail validation.

# CONTROL AUTHORITY

While running, rawpanel owns the per-screen selection
*\_RAWPANEL\_CONTROL\_Sn*. The selection owner advertises version and supported
commands. Visibility control is always advertised. Native volume commands are
advertised only while the status worker has one enabled, unambiguous ALSA
source; they are withdrawn if that worker is lost. This boundary is intended for
independent input routers; selection loss is authoritative process loss.

# SEE ALSO

*rawpanel.conf*(5), *rawm*(1), *rawctl*(1)
